    ".WML",
    "Wireless Markup Language File",
    "3.3",
    "Web page created for mobile devices, such as PDAs (personal digital assistants) and cell phones; similar to an.HTML file, but written in the wireless markup language (WML) instead of HTML. The wireless markup language is part of the the Wireless Application Protocol (WAP). WML files may include WMLScript, which is a light version of JavaScript. They can be opened in a WML-compatible Web browser or with a WML-enabled mobile device. Windows Adobe Dreamweaver 2021. SyncRO Soft oXygen XML Editor. AbiSource AbiWord. Microsoft Internet Explorer. Google Chrome. Mozilla Firefox. Other Web browser Mac Adobe Dreamweaver 2021. SyncRO Soft oXygen XML Editor. Apple Safari Included with OS. Google Chrome. Mozilla Firefox. Other Web browser Linux SyncRO Soft oXygen XML Editor. Google Chrome. Mozilla Firefox. Other Web browser.",
    "Windows Adobe Dreamweaver 2021. SyncRO Soft oXygen XML Editor. AbiSource AbiWord. Microsoft Internet Explorer. Google Chrome. Mozilla Firefox. Other Web browser. Mac Adobe Dreamweaver 2021. SyncRO Soft oXygen XML Editor. Apple Safari Included with OS. Google Chrome. Mozilla Firefox. Other Web browser. Linux SyncRO Soft oXygen XML Editor. Google Chrome. Mozilla Firefox. Other Web browser.",
