    ".CODASITE",
    "Coda Site File",
    "3.0",
    "Website project file created by Coda, a program used for creating and publishing webpages; stores the list of Web files for the project (i.e.,.HTML,.CSS,.JS, and other supported types); also includes the publishing information for the remote server. When you create a new site profile in Coda, a CODASITE file is saved to the ~/​Library/​Application Support/​Coda 2/​Sites/​ directory. NOTE: Coda sites are managed through the Coda user interface and therefore CODASITE files are not manually opened by the user from the Mac Finder. Mac Panic Coda 2.",
