    ".PHP3",
    "PHP 3 Web Page",
    "2.6",
    "Web page that may contain PHP 3 code; the PHP code within the page is parsed by a PHP engine on the Web server, which dynamically generates HTML that is sent to the users Web browser; often used in combination with a database, such as MySQL. PHP3 pages can be processed by Apache, Windows Server, or Mac OS X Server with the PHP engine installed. They can be edited with a text editor or Web development program. PHP pages generally use the.PHP file extension. Windows PHP. Apache Web Server with PHP. Eclipse PHP Development Tools. Adobe Dreamweaver 2021. ES-Computing EditPlus. gVim. Any Web browser Mac PHP. Apache Web Server with PHP. Eclipse PHP Development Tools. Adobe Dreamweaver 2021. MacroMates TextMate. Any Web browser Linux PHP. Apache Web Server with PHP. Eclipse PHP Development Tools. VimFree.",
