    ["web_files",
    ".PPTHTML",
    "Microsoft PowerPoint HTML Presentation",
    "2.2",
    "A PPTHTML file is an HTML version of a.PPT file created with Microsoft PowerPoint, a program used for creating presentations. It contains HTML that can be used to display the presentation with formatting similar to the original PPT file. PPTHTML files are primarily used for viewing published presentations in a web browser. Microsoft PowerPoint no longer supports the PPTHTML format. Instead of saving documents as PPTHTML files, you can share presentations online by selecting Slide Show → Present Online in PowerPoint 365. This option allows you to publish your presentation online where others can view it in a web browser. Unfortunately, there are no known applications that fully support the PPTHTML format since Microsoft PowerPoint dropped support for it. Windows No longer supported by Microsoft PowerPoint Mac No longer supported by Microsoft PowerPoint.",
    "Windows No longer supported by Microsoft PowerPoint. Mac No longer supported by Microsoft PowerPoint.",
    "?"],
    ["web_files",
    ".STM",
    "SSI Web Page",
    "2.1",
    "An STM file is an audio tracking module file saved in the Scream Tracker Module (STM) format, a proprietary format used by versions 1 and 2 of Scream Tracker. It contains tracks, patterns, and samples used for instruments played back in the songs. STM file open in OpenMPT 1 Future Crew developed the first version of Scream Tracker in the late-1980s to modify the popular.MOD Amiga Module format introduced in 1987. Future Crew then released version 2 of Scream Tracker in 1990. The STM format is the default format that Scream Tracker 1 and 2 use to save music. However, future Crew eventually replaced the STM format with the Scream Tracker 3 Module (S3M) format when it released Scream Tracker 3 in 1994. Even though Future Crew discontinued Scream Tracker in the 1990s, you may still encounter old STM files created by the original application. You may also acquire STM files created by music enthusiasts using a third-party application that supports the STM format. You can open an STM file with many audio applications, such as OpenMPT (Windows), Nullsoft Winamp (Windows), MikMod (multiplatform), and Schism Tracker (multiplatform). For example, you can open an STM file with OpenMPT by selecting File → Open... Mac Schism Tracker. MikMod. CocoModX —  (Discontinued). Windows OpenMPT. Schism Tracker. Nullsoft Winamp. MikMod. Linux Schism TrackerFree. Data file saved by Microsoft Exchange Server in conjunction with.EDB files; used by the Exchange information store, which is comprised of:. Priv1.edb Priv1.stm Pub1.edb Pub1.stm STM files store streamed native Internet content. New messages are saved to the STM file on the mail server until they are accessed by a users mail client. When messages are accessed by a MAPI client, they are transferred to the EDB file and converted to the native Exchange format. Windows Microsoft Exchange Server. Stellar Repair for Exchange. An STM file contains a stamp created by The Powder Toy, a free 2D physics simulation sandbox game. It stores a stamp, which is a customized area selected and saved in The Powder Toy during gameplay. STM files are considered mini-saves that can be used to make up a larger simulation save in the game, which is stored in the.CPS file. STM file open in hardWIRED The Powder Toy 92.5 The Powder Toy allows you to play with different substances to simulate the effects of different property interactions. The game comes with a variety of liquids, gases, electronic components, and building materials that you can use to build terrains, explosives, buildings, and more. During gameplay you can set a specified area to be saved and loaded at a different time. The elements or objects in the specified area are included in the save. These saved areas are called stamps and are stored in the STM file. To create an STM file, type S during gameplay and draw the area you want to save as a stamp. To load an STM file, type K during gameplay and choose the stamp you want to load. Mac hardWIRED The Powder Toy. Windows hardWIRED The Powder Toy. Linux hardWIRED The Powder ToyFree. Web page that contains server side includes (SSI); references functions on the server that generates content for the Web page; processed by the server when accessed, which outputs HTML to clients Web browser. Server Side Include Web pages may also use the.SHTM or.SHTML extensions. Mac Any Web browser Run on a Web server Windows Any Web browser Run on a Web server.",
    "Mac Schism Tracker. MikMod. CocoModX —  (Discontinued). Windows OpenMPT. Schism Tracker. Nullsoft Winamp. MikMod. Linux Schism Tracker. Windows Microsoft Exchange Server. Stellar Repair for Exchange. Mac hardWIRED The Powder Toy. Windows hardWIRED The Powder Toy. Linux hardWIRED The Powder Toy. Mac Any Web browser Run on a Web server. Windows Any Web browser Run on a Web server.",
    "OpenMPT can convert STM files to the following formats:.MID - MIDI File.IT - Impulse Tracker Module.WAV - WAVE Audio File.FLAC -. Lossless Audio Codec File.AU - Audacity Audio File.OPUS - Opus Audio File.OGG - Ogg Vorbis Audio File.RAW - Raw Audio Data.MP3 - MP3 Audio File."],
