    ["web_files",
    ".CPG",
    "Cool Page Project File",
    "2.0",
    "Character encoding file used by ESRI software products such as the ArcGIS Desktop suite; describes a set of characters for displaying text in shapefiles; helps localize maps for specific languages. Windows ESRI ArcGIS Pro. Page file created by Manga Studio, a program used to create digital comic art; contains page layout settings as well as cartoon sketches, textures, captions, word balloons, and special effects; can be exported to.BMP,.JPG,.PSD,.PNG,.TIFF,.TGA, and.PICT formats. Manga Studio became Clip Studio Paint in 2015. It is also known as ComicStudio in Japan. Windows CELSYS Clip Studio Paint Pro. Mac CELSYS Clip Studio Paint Pro. Campaign file for StarCraft, a real-time strategy game that takes place in space; includes mission data and artificial intelligence information, which determines the difficulty of the mission. NOTE: StarCraft maps are saved as.SCM files. Windows Blizzard StarCraft. Mac Blizzard StarCraft. Web page project created by Cool Page, an older drag and drop Web page editor; may contain various Web page objects and their properties; allows users to save designed pages. Since CPG files are saved in a proprietary format, they can only be opened in Cool Page. However, these files can be published to standard HTML. NOTE: The last version of Cool Page was released in 2002, and the last supported operating system was Windows XP. Windows 3Dize Cool Page. A CPG file is a codeplug file used by a Motorola Solutions two-way radio. It contains channel settings and other data used to program a radio. CPG files are radio-specific, and they are edited using Motorola Solutions customer programming software (CPS). Motorola Solutions two-way radio users who want to adjust the frequencies their radio operates upon can do so by loading and editing the radios CPG file in a CPS program. For example, a user with access to the MOTOTRBO CPS can connect their radio to their computer and use MOTOTRBO to READ and edit their radios CPG file. A radios CPG file also contains other information specific to that radio. For example, the CPG file lists the radios serial number and FLASHcode features. Because a radios CPG file contains so much essential data, and editing the file incorrectly can cause your radio to malfunction, it is recommended that you save a backup of your radios original CPG file before editing it. That way, you can re-install your radios original CPG file if needed. The following Motorola Solutions two-way radios are known to use CPG format codeplugs. HT750 HT1250 MTX9250. You can open and edit a CPG file in Motorola Solutions MOTOTRBO CPS (Windows), which must be purchased from Motorola. After purchasing and installing MOTOTRBO, open the program, select Open from its toolbar, and then navigate to and open your CPG file. Windows Motorola Solutions MOTOTRBO CPS.",
    "Windows ESRI ArcGIS Pro. Windows CELSYS Clip Studio Paint Pro. Mac CELSYS Clip Studio Paint Pro. Windows Blizzard StarCraft. Mac Blizzard StarCraft. Windows 3Dize Cool Page. Windows Motorola Solutions MOTOTRBO CPS.",
    "?"],
