    ".WPX",
    "WebPlus Project Template",
    "2.0",
    "Printer information file that contains a description of the printers features; may be referenced when printer jobs are created and sent to the printer; often installed with Windows PostScript printers. WPX files typically take up about 12K of disk space and are stored in the /WINDOWS or /WINDOWS/SYSTEM directory. Windows Referenced by the Windows operating system Mac Parallels Desktop for Mac with Windows installed. Project template used by WebPlus, a Web design program; enables new projects (.WPP files) to be created with a preformatted look and feel; may include default graphics, text, and layout settings for one or more pages. WPX files enable Web developers to download and share website templates. This makes it easier to bootstrap a website since the initial design does not have to be created from scratch. NOTE: Serif no longer develops WebPlus. The last version of the program was X8 and discontinued in 2016. Windows Serif WebPlus.",
